      "text": [
        " : قُلْتُ لِأَبِي عَبْدِ اَللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ إِنَّ وَالِدَتِي تُوُفِّيَتْ وَ لَمْ تَحُجَّ قَالَ «يَحُجُّ عَنْهَا رَجُلٌ أَوِ اِمْرَأَةٌ» قَالَ قُلْتُ أَيُّهُمْ أَحَبُّ إِلَيْكَ قَالَ «رَجُلٌ أَحَبُّ إِلَيَّ »."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.2921 - It was narrated from Basheer al-Nabbal, who said:\nI said to Abu Abdullah (as): \"My mother passed away and did not perform Hajj.\"\nImam (as) said: \"A man or a woman may perform Hajj on her behalf.\"\nI asked: \"Which is more preferable to you?\"\nImam (as) said: \"A man is more preferable to me.\""
        ]
      }
